            "review_title": "Review at MJL Food Center",
            "review_text": "Ryan L\n21 contributions\n0\nGreat food; strange, abusive owner.\nOct 2017 • Solo\nTo be fair, the food here is pretty decent for a hole-in-the wall off of Thao Dien. The curries are fantastic and the rice come in heaping, delicious servings. My only gripe is with the owner; the only female lumbering around the shop. She behaves strangely and seems to go out of her way to get rude with me. Once I asked her about one of the employees (I was ignorant as to his position in the company) and she replied with an annoyed, almost shrieking tone: \"NOOOO!!! He's just a HELPAAAA!!!!!\". The second strange experience was just last night; she placed my food to go on the counter, though right next to someone else's food to go. I paid and grabbed both of them (I ordered 2 things anyway) and was out the door. She caught up with me outside and asked if I took 2 bags, I said \"yes\", and she said I took someone's food in this tone that went from friendly to snide and abusive in under a second. I thought to myself why would you put my food together with another person's and then get offended when I accidentally take it? I threw the food back to her and drove away. Great food, useless owner.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 5, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
